+## Cause review and offline report binding
+
+The existing builder reports `gateP`, `creditedAllClasses` and `allAttempts` separately. Counts are classified-event claims; verified totals require complete bound independent review, otherwise total is null. Earlier excluded attempts and all original false-pass/leak facts remain. Code checks exact bindings and closed types; it does not authenticate a reviewer, infer causal truth from a name/hash, or supply actual independent QA adoption. Generic BUDGET_EXCEEDED, page marks, successful sessions, missing canaries and display hints never establish cause or absence.
+
+`benchmark-report` config names `manifest`, optional `corpusRoot`, pinned `rawRuns` and `causeAnnotations` references, `reviews` references, `independentQaAdoption`, `originalExecution`, the original-start `admissionLedger` and separate `intervalAdmissionLedger`. Each reference is `{path,sha256}` over exact file bytes. Raw original JSONL is never rewritten. The annotation header binds its hash; exactly one ordinal/canonical-record-hash/manifest/case/rep/attempt annotation covers every original position, including UNKNOWN. Only cause counts, cause-event arrays and causeAssessment may differ; events/counts already present cannot decrease. Non-cause details, completion/oracle/hard facts, modes, infra, timestamps, sessions and counters stay original. Disputed raw facts need a separately authorized successor retaining their original claims.
+
+Closed review records bind each cause, original raw record, authored-goal/outcome/location pins and justified observation scope. Independent adoption must cover those exact records and actual original execution/configuration evidence. A hash-shaped claim alone stays UNKNOWN/non-adoptable. The CLI preserves original/refusal artifacts and writes only a fresh destination. HARNESS_SELF_TEST cannot become D_C. The admission reference must identify the immutable original-time ledger snapshot (future live output `admission-ledger.json`), not a later mutable ledger substituted as permission. It verifies the effective original entry and admittedAt before the execution start and every included D_C run. Legacy missing original receipt/snapshot/provenance remains UNBOUND/refused; no rescore-time timestamp or inferred limits identity repairs it. Later ledger entries neither admit earlier work nor rewrite its retained snapshot. The original receipt must additionally bind the actual original `finishedAt` and exact `intervalLedgerSha256`; the independent adoption must bind that terminal history and affirm its actual original interval was reviewed. The terminal history must preserve the complete original-start snapshot as an exact prefix, cover every original raw run finish, and contain no same-purpose STOP, refusal or changed admission anywhere from original execution start through its end. STOP followed by re-admission cannot restore the interrupted single history; endpoint ADMITTED alone is insufficient. Other-purpose entries alone and entries strictly after the bound original end do not constitute an interval interruption. Raw `runFinishedAt` ISO validation remains required. Missing or unbound authoritative end/history stays UNKNOWN/non-adoptable, never filled with a start timestamp, rescore/report clock, guessed duration or later permission.
+
+Future live CLI output preserves `admission-ledger.json` as the original start snapshot, samples an actual closure time after the original run returns, and reads separate terminal ledger bytes into `admission-ledger-interval.json` when available. Its unreviewed receipt binds those exact bytes and the actual sampled end; neither a start snapshot nor this terminal read alone authenticates complete original history. Independent adoption must establish that actual authoritative coverage. Missing ledger/end/receipt facts, process death and legacy captures remain UNKNOWN; no durable journal, producer recovery or legacy provenance is invented.
+
+Learn sessions preserve separate base/suffix facts. Each started learn is charged once; a base failure, leak or existing stop starts no suffix. A partial repetition retains real base SUCCEEDED with whole published:false and explicit incomplete oracle; base success alone is not a final false pass. Later hard facts share the existing latch without charging again. The three scopes expose logical attempts, known started sessions, unknown scope, per-value known subtotals and null incomplete totals. An empty population is not observed zero; an affirmative complete no-start record can establish zero. Public proposal/reservation counters and conservative/fallback stop charges remain `PUBLIC_BUDGET_COUNTERS`/named protective bases. Proposals are not actual wire calls. Actual provider tokens/cost remain null/UNAVAILABLE; this code does not manufacture ED-01 or MODEL-SIZING per-call evidence.
